ng `i % xs.length` elements from the start of the list\nto the end.\n\nThis is the implementation of `List.rotateLeft` used at runtime; it is compiled using\n`List.takeTR`.","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.rotateLeftTR","kind":"def","line":287,"name":"List.rotateLeftTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L287-L302"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.extract_eq_extractTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">extract_eq_extractTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\">@<a href=\"./Init/Data/List/Basic.html#List.extract\">extract</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> @<a href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.extractTR\">extractTR</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.extract_eq_extractTR","kind":"theorem","line":282,"name":"List.extract_eq_extractTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L282-L283"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.extractTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">extractTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">l</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">start</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a> := <span class=\"fn\">0</span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">stop</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a> := <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">l</span>.<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List.length\">length</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the slice of `l` from indices `start` (inclusive) to `stop` (exclusive).\n\nThis is the implementation of `List.extract` used at runtime; it is compiled using `List.takeTR`.","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.extractTR","kind":"def","line":274,"name":"List.extractTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L274-L280"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.take_eq_takeTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">take_eq_takeTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\">@<a href=\"./Init/Data/List/Basic.html#List.take\">take</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> @<a href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.takeTR\">takeTR</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.take_eq_takeTR","kind":"theorem","line":261,"name":"List.take_eq_takeTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L261-L270"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.takeTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">takeTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">l</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Extracts the first `n` elements of `xs`, or the whole list if `n` is greater than `xs.length`.\n\n`O(min n |xs|)`. This is a tail-recursive version of `List.take`, used at runtime.\n\nExamples:\n* `[a, b, c, d, e].takeTR 0 = []`\n* `[a, b, c, d, e].takeTR 3 = [a, b, c]`\n* `[a, b, c, d, e].takeTR 6 = [a, b, c, d, e]`","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.takeTR","kind":"def","line":243,"name":"List.takeTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L243-L259"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flatten_eq_flattenTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">flatten_eq_flattenTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\">@<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List.flatten\">flatten</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> @<a href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flattenTR\">flattenTR</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flatten_eq_flattenTR","kind":"theorem","line":236,"name":"List.flatten_eq_flattenTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L236-L237"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flattenTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">flattenTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">l</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span>)</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Concatenates a list of lists into a single list, preserving the order of the elements.\n\n`O(|flatten L|)`. This is a tail-recursive version of `List.flatten`, used in runtime code.\n\nExamples:\n* `[[\"a\"], [\"b\", \"c\"]].flattenTR = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]`\n* `[[\"a\"], [], [\"b\", \"c\"], [\"d\", \"e\", \"f\"]].flattenTR = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\", \"e\", \"f\"]`","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flattenTR","kind":"def","line":225,"name":"List.flattenTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L225-L234"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flatMap_eq_flatMapTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">flatMap_eq_flatMapTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\">@<a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List.flatMap\">flatMap</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Eq\">=</a> @<a href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flatMapTR\">flatMapTR</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flatMap_eq_flatMapTR","kind":"theorem","line":216,"name":"List.flatMap_eq_flatMapTR","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Init/Data/List/Impl.lean#L216-L221"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flatMapTR\"><span class=\"name\">List</span>.<span class=\"name\">flatMapTR</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">β</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_2}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">α</span> → <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">as</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List\">List</a> <span class=\"fn\">β</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Applies a function that returns a list to each element of a list, and concatenates the resulting\nlists.\n\nThis is the tail-recursive version of `List.flatMap` that's used at runtime.\n\nExamples:\n* `[2, 3, 2].flatMapTR List.range = [0, 1, 0, 1, 2, 0, 1]`\n* `[\"red\", \"blue\"].flatMapTR String.toList = ['r', 'e', 'd', 'b', 'l', 'u', 'e']`","docLink":"./Init/Data/List/Impl.html#List.flatMapTR","kind":"def","line":200,"name":"List.flatMapTR","sourceLink":"https://gi